  "one_mechanism": {
    "summary": "One Slime placement rule combines the moon-threshold surface path with a deterministic eligible chunk and separate underground attempt draw.",
    "surface": "Non-Peaceful, tagged biome and Y 51–69. Three random checks compose a 0.5F roll, roll below dimension moon brightness by world day, and raw brightness at most nextInt(8). No independent isNight() gate is in the predicate. Passing the environmental condition returns the ordinary supporting-block result immediately.",
    "underground": "The level accessor must implement WorldGenLevel; ordinary ServerLevel does. WorldgenRandom fixes world seed, chunk X/Z and salt 987234911 to a distinct LegacyRandomSource. The Java int products before casts wrap even where a later term is multiplied as long. Eligible chunk draw, separate server attempt draw, Y <40 and support must all pass. No surface-tag or local brightness check here.",
    "runtime": "SLIME is MONSTER with ON_GROUND. A selected effective spawn table, physical placement, Forge placement/PositionCheck, collision and true admission are distinct. The raw base tag only comprises swamp and mangrove swamp; matching placement in other biomes can use the underground path when their effective table has Slime. No implications for the current Dynasty CREATURE denominator or actual admission.",
