    "verbatim_text": "**Verdict: one distinct ecology candidate.** Review the surface and underground branches as one Slime placement mechanism. The distinctive behavior is a stable, world-seeded chunk filter with a separate per-attempt roll, alongside a surface path gated by moon phase. This is static evidence. The recorded baselines remain **83/1000** formal references, **24/30** native births, and **9/10** same-UUID pickups. [Latest ecology continuation](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/resume-20261120/general-specialist-ecology-proof-repairs-20261126.json:4)\n\n- **Surface.** `Slime.java:261–265` requires non-Peaceful difficulty, a tagged biome, Y **51–69**, a 50% roll, a second roll below moon brightness, and raw local brightness at or below `nextInt(8)`. It then checks the supporting block through `Mob.java:831–834`. Moon brightness comes from world day time (`LevelTimeAccess.java:8–9`, `DimensionType.java:36,101–103`). The vanilla tag lists swamp and mangrove swamp. Both biome tables contain `MONSTER` Slime rows of weight 100 for groups of four and weight 1 for singletons. Either row can feed the same predicate. [Exact Slime source](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/art/bestiary-v43/drowner-slime-squish-consumer-whole-research-20261112/sources/Slime.java:261)\n- **Underground.** `Slime.java:267–274` requires `WorldGenLevel`, Y **<40**, a deterministic `nextInt(10)==0` result from world seed, chunk X/Z and salt `987234911L`, plus a separate `nextInt(10)==0` attempt roll and the supporting-block check. This branch has no light or surface-tag test. `WorldgenRandom.java:70–72` fixes the seed arithmetic, including Java `int` overflow before the casts. The live `ServerLevel` implements `WorldGenLevel` and supplies the world seed (`ServerLevel.java:160,1370–1372`). [Exact Slime source](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/art/bestiary-v43/drowner-slime-squish-consumer-whole-research-20261112/sources/Slime.java:267)\n- **Deduplication.** EA-0002 searches for one habitat chunk and persists the result or give-up state. Slime recomputes eligibility for each queried chunk. EA-0007 overlaps on habitat and rarity checks. Its shared configurable predicate does not contain the seeded chunk and lunar alternatives. EA-0043’s time-of-day check controls a tame cat’s owner-sleep gift. The legacy `seedSlimeChunk` row is an unreviewed helper candidate. The accepted legacy Slime row covers size restoration and death splitting, the art copy covers squish rendering, and Narslimmus uses the chunk test to mark an already selected spawn for flower eligibility. [EA-0002](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/batch-001.json:310) · [EA-0007](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/batch-002.json:1137) · [EA-0043](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/batch-034.json:23) · [Legacy helper](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/legacy-migration-acceptance/candidates.jsonl:16509) · [Legacy Slime owner](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/legacy-migration-acceptance/reviewed.jsonl:710) · [Art study](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/art/bestiary-v43/drowner-slime-squish-consumer-whole-research-20261112/whole-study.json:7) · [Narslimmus](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/todo-evidence-review-20261101/next-owner-narslimmus-triage44-zero-20261101.json:86)\n- **Runtime boundary.** Slime is registered as `MONSTER` with `ON_GROUND` placement (`EntityType.java:256`, `SpawnPlacements.java:113`), so this does not address the `CREATURE` cap. `NaturalSpawner.java:106–108,208–222,244–263` puts category budget, effective spawn-table selection, geometry, and Forge placement and position arbitration around the predicate. `NaturalSpawner.java:330–332` selects `CREATURE` for vanilla chunk-generation spawning. A `NATURAL` placement pass or finalize event alone cannot prove admission. A runtime receipt needs the same fresh entity admitted and observed alive on a later `ServerLevel` tick. [Forge admission evidence](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/general-tropical-fish-forge-redirect-and-birth-proof-20261126.json:412)\n\nBoth cached paths and SHA-256 hashes matched the source receipt. The mapped Forge archive was `1b3fbc4e77b7523058b8c03ee4c9f8d9db2a6c9bb41f4afc5277f968ad1070e0`, and the vanilla data archive was `f43d1ac034a8907edab190a17501fd4ca2b0af107d4231da364eeca8ab5ee317`. Review was offline and read-only on Dynasty `main`. [Archive paths and expected hashes](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/general-tropical-fish-native-school-finalization-source-review-20261125.json:32)",
